  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 22. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. 貸出 — 本や道具などを貸すこと。\n2. 菓子屋 — お菓子を売る店。\n3. 歌集 — 短歌や歌などを集めた本。\n4. 箇所 — ある特定の場所や部分。\n5. 頭文字 — 言葉や名前の最初の文字。\n6. 河川敷 — 川の流れと堤防の間にある平らな土地。\n7. 風通し — 風が通り抜ける具合。\n8. 肩書き — 役職や身分などを表す名前。\n9. 片側 — 二つあるうちの一つの側。\n10. 肩こり — 肩の筋肉がこわばって重く感じること。\n11. 硬さ — 物が形を変えにくい度合い。\n12. 片隅 — 場所のすみの方。\n13. 片方 — 二つのうちの一つ。\n14. 偏り — 一方に多く集まってつり合わないこと。\n15. 語り手 — 物語や体験などを話す人。\n16. 勝ち越し — 試合などで負けた数より勝った数が多いこと。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\n",
